    "body": "**Describe the bug**\r\nThe simorgh consent banner sets cookies to `www.bbc.com` whereas the pal sets them to `.bbc.com`. This causes weird behaviour where we read from 1 domain, but write to another. This means the cookie banner cant be dismissed in some cases\r\n\r\n**Unconfirmed:**\r\nIt appears that our cookie banner will read cookies set on `.bbc.com` and set cookies on `www.bbc.com`, which means you cant correct the values, and it will show the banners on every refresh\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\nSteps to reproduce the behavior:\r\n\r\nOn Chrome and Firefox \r\n1. Go to bbc.com/pidgin\r\n2. Click on \"Yes I agree\" to the cookie settings\r\n3. Refresh the page\r\n4. See the cookie banner is displayed again \r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\nWhen you \"Yes click I agree\" then you don't see the cookie banner again when the page is refreshed\r\n\r\nSimorgh sets cookies the same place that the pal does\r\n\r\n\r\n**Screenshots**\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/11341355/63882037-0de17680-c9c9-11e9-8be8-4873379334d8.png)\r\n\r\n**Testing notes**\r\n\r\n- [x] This bug fix is expected to need manual testing.\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\nAdd any other context about the problem here.\r\n",
